# The release signing key and its password, in plaintext — permanent app
# identity, never committed. android/app/build.gradle's release signingConfig
# reads keystore.properties from here (see its comment for why the path is
# what it is).
credentials/

# android/ and ios/ are intentionally NOT blanket-ignored: they hold hand-
# maintained native code (AppDelegate.swift, Info.plist, build.gradle) that
# has to be committed for anyone else's checkout — or CI — to build the app,
# same as any other Capacitor project. Each has its own nested .gitignore
# (android/.gitignore, ios/.gitignore) scoped to their generated build
# artifacts (Pods/, build/, .gradle/, xcuserdata, copied web assets) — that's
# what actually keeps the noise out, and a parent-level blanket ignore here
# would silently defeat it by never letting git walk into either directory.
